# ParserTrace conventions

### Category hierarchy

Group prefixes enable entire groups. Leaves enable one stream. Full list
lives in `docs/06_DEVELOPER_EXPERIENCE.md`; `meridian trace categories` prints it live.

| Enum case | Raw value (CLI / env var string) |
|---|---|
| `.tokenize` | `tokenize` |
| `.parse` | `parse` |
| `.phraseParse` | `phrase.parse` |
| `.phraseMatch` | `phrase.match` |
| `.phraseExtractArgs` | `phrase.args` |
| `.phraseInline` | `phrase.inline` |
| `.statement` | `statement` |
| `.expression` | `expression` |
| `.lowering` | `lowering` |
| `.symbols` | `symbols` |
| `.merconfig` | `merconfig` |
| `.rulebook` | `rulebook` |
| `.skill` | `skill` |
| `.codegen` | `codegen` |
| `.verbalizer` | `verbalizer` |
| `.validation` | `validation` |
| `.drift` | `drift` |
| `.diagnostics` | `diagnostics` |
| `.timing` | `timing` (off by default; excluded from `capturing()`'s default set) |

`.diagnostics` mirrors every `DiagnosticEngine`-reported `Diagnostic` into the
trace stream. `.timing` accumulates `trace.phase(_:)` spans (bootstrap
sub-phases, `symbols`/`parse`/`lower`, post-lower `domainDecl` /
`traceIdentity.*` / `obligationStamp`, `codegen`/`codegen-multi`,
`manifestRules`/`obligationDocument`, multi-source `compile (N file(s))`) and prints
an end-of-compile profile; it's opt-in only, so `ParserTrace.capturing()` (no
explicit `categories:`) never includes it — pass `categories: [.timing]` explicitly to
assert timing output.

### `MERIDIAN_TRACE` env var

`ParserTrace()` reads `MERIDIAN_TRACE` **at init time** and auto-enables
categories. Both `ParserTrace.shared` and fresh `ParserTrace()` instances
read this env var. This means:
- Setting `MERIDIAN_TRACE=all swift test` activates tracing globally for that
  test run.
- Tests that create `ParserTrace()` will inherit env-var activation unless
  they call `disableAll()` explicitly.
- Use `ParserTrace.silent()` in tests that want guaranteed silence regardless
  of env var.

CLI bootstrap (`makeCLITrace` in `CLISupport.swift`) calls `announceCLITrace`
when **any** category is enabled after init — including env-only activation
with no `--trace` flag. The banner is always:
`trace correlation id: <uuid> (JSONL records include "corr")`.

### Thread safety

`ParserTrace` is `@unchecked Sendable` with internal `NSLock` for all mutable
state. Span stacks and indent levels are keyed by `ObjectIdentifier(Thread.current)`
so concurrent compiles on one trace instance stay balanced. It is safe to call
`log/push/pop/openSpan/closeSpan` from concurrent contexts. In unit tests,
prefer a fresh `ParserTrace.capturing(…).trace` per test to avoid cross-test
output mixing.

### Structured spans

`openSpan`/`closeSpan` are the canonical scope API; `push`/`pop` delegate to
them. Each `ParserTrace` instance gets a stable `correlationID` (UUID) and
assigns monotonic `sequence` numbers to emitted records. `Token` carries
`spanID`, `parentSpanID`, `active`, `cat`, and optional `sequence`.
`outputFormat = .jsonl` emits one JSON object per line (`seq`, `corr`, `span`,
`parent`, `cat`, `op`, `kind`, `outcome?`, `msg`, `range?`); default `.text`
preserves `[category] …` lines with `▶`/`◀` markers.

- **Zero-cost when disabled:** `openSpan`/`closeSpan`/`log`/`detail` return
  immediately when the category is off (no string work, no I/O).
- **Per-thread nesting:** span stacks keyed by `ObjectIdentifier(Thread.current)`.
- **CLI:** `--trace-format text|jsonl` via `CLITraceOptions` on every command
  that runs compile/migration/analysis tooling (`compile`, `check`, `verify`,
  `run`, `lint`, `explain`, `drift`, `migrate-skill`, …). Active tracing
  (from `--trace` or `MERIDIAN_TRACE`) prints `trace correlation id: …` once
  on stderr (`announceCLITrace`).
- **`.validation`:** `IRValidator` uses `openSpan(.validation, …)` /
  `closeSpan(…, outcome:)` — enable for pre-emission IR checks.
- **Post-lower:** `Compiler.annotateAndStampObligations` times
  `traceIdentity.hash`, `traceIdentity.annotate`, `obligationStamp` and logs
  `.codegen` summaries; `compile(_:)` also times `domainDecl`,
  `manifestRules`, `obligationDocument`. See `docs/06_DEVELOPER_EXPERIENCE.md` phase map.
- **Lint:** `LintCommand` uses `@OptionGroup var traceOptions: CLITraceOptions`;
  `trace.run { MeridianLinter().lint(…) }` lets the tokenizer read the
  task-local and opens a `lint <file>` span under `.diagnostics`.

### Adding a trace point

1. Optionally add a new `Category` case and its `rawValue` string.
2. Call `trace.log(.category, "…")` or `trace.push/pop` in the relevant method.
3. Add a `capturing(categories:)` test to `ParserTraceTests.swift`.

### The task-local trace convention

The active trace is a task-local — compiler components do **not** take a
`trace:` parameter:

```swift
@TaskLocal public static var current: ParserTrace = .shared
```

- **Injection point 1 — `Compiler.Options.trace`:** every `Compiler` entry
  point (`compile(_:)`, `bootstrap(_:)`, `emit(workflows:)`,
  `emitManifest(_:)`) installs `options.trace` as `ParserTrace.current` for the
  duration of the call; the whole pipeline sees it with no threading.
- **Injection point 2 — `trace.run { … }`:** wrap a direct API call
  (parser/emitter/linter/verbalizer used outside a compile). An async `run`
  overload exists for `await`ed bodies.
- Hot paths (`IndentTokenizer.tokenize`, `StatementParser` entry points,
  `ExpressionParser.parse`, `ASTToIR.lowerWorkflow`, `SwiftEmitter.emit`,
  `DiagnosticEngine.report`) read `ParserTrace.current` once per entry call
  into a local, not per loop iteration.
- `@TaskLocal` values are inherited by child tasks; `Task.detached` does not
  inherit (nothing in the compiler detaches).
- The CLI never mutates `.shared`: `compile`, `check`, `verify`, `run`,
  `lint`, `migrate-skill`, `preview-skill`, `explain`, `drift`, `inert-yield`, and
  `skill-deviation` each build a fresh, isolated instance via
  `makeCLITrace(spec:file:format:)` (`Sources/MeridianCLIKit/CLISupport.swift`)
  from their `@OptionGroup` `CLITraceOptions` (`--trace`, `--trace-file`,
  `--trace-format`), pass it through `Compiler.Options.trace`, and wrap any
  direct-API work in `traceInstance.run { … }`.
- Tests: pass `cap.trace` through `Compiler.Options` when driving a compile;
  wrap direct type calls in `cap.trace.run { … }` (async variant for async
  bodies). Captures are per-task, so parallel suites cannot leak into each
  other.

### No silent-trace components

Nothing in the compile pipeline is allowed to hardcode `.silent()` — that would
silently discard a caller's `--trace` request. Only test call sites may pass
`.silent()` explicitly.

Production-source exceptions must stay on the machine-checked allowlist in
`docs/coverage/SILENT_FALLBACK_ALLOWLIST.md`: `TrialLowering` and
`InertYieldAnalyzer` probe paths, plus `ParserBenchmark` benchmark noise
control. Do not add another `.silent()` in `Sources/` without adding an
allowlist entry and a reason.

Trace emission redacts obvious secrets before writing to any sink:
authorization headers, bearer tokens, password/API-key fields, and `secret=...`
style fields become `<redacted>`.

### Strict-by-default fallbacks

Compile-time default is `FallbackPolicy.strict` (empty `allowed` set). Opt-in
only via frontmatter `allow-fallbacks:` (`FallbackKind` tokens) or
`Compiler.Options.fallbackPolicy = .lenient`. Every allowed fallback emits a
warning diagnostic plus a `.lowering` trace line. Deontic conditions have no
fallback — unlowerable norms raise `MER-DEO-007`. See `docs/06_DEVELOPER_EXPERIENCE.md`
§"Strict-by-default fallback policy".
